--
Wrong verdict: `S()` for a class with default member initializers but no
user-provided constructor produced the all-zero value (the class is a POD to
the front end and the functional cast zero-initialized it), so `S c = S();`
had c.v == 0 and the assertion `c.v == 3` FAILED.  Value-initialization now
zero-initializes the temporary and runs the synthesized default constructor
over it ([dcl.init.general]/9.1).  Non-vacuous: the last assertion states a
wrong value and must FAIL.
